{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1532499-exalted-caste-simile-with-atlantean-orders","id":1532499,"title":"Exalted Caste Simile with Atlantean Orders","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-03-13T07:58:43-07:00","id":1532499,"title":"Exalted Caste Simile with Atlantean Orders","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> I understand that Exalted and Mage are mechanically, metaphysically, and cosmologically different. But I can not help to compare them in the type of awakened that Supernal Realms bring:<ul><li>Solars: Obrimos</li> <li>Infernals: Mastigos</li> <li>Abyssals: Moros</li> <li>Sideral: Acanthus</li> <li>Lunar: Thyrsus</li> </ul><br /> Now, at least the Solars castes and their derivatives, look similar to the traditional Orders roles:<ul><li>Dawn / Dusk / Slayer: Adamantine Arrow.</li> <li>Zenith / Midnight / Malefactor: Silver Ladder.</li> <li>Twilight / Daybreak / Malefactor: Mysterium.</li> <li>Night / Day / Scourge: Guardians of the Veil.</li> </ul>Where in that analogy are the Eclipse / Moonshadow / Fiends??? The do not seem to my eyes to be Free Coucil-ish and will be also similar to the Silver Ladder.<br /> <br /> Thanks,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 03-13-2024, 04:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-13T09:59:33-07:00","id":1532510,"title":"","content":"Bad analogy. The Orders aren't <i>roles.</i> They're religions, philosophies, and teaching traditions. (The aesthetics are deceptive, too. The demons of Pandemonium are the <i>inner demons</i> of your own mind, the thoughts that torment you but which are ultimately integral to who you are and necessary to help you grow as a person. Exalted doesn't really <i>have</i> angels, and Sidereals and fate aren't associated with the Fair Folk.)<br /> <br /> An Adamantine Arrow will usually be in some kind of confrontational or martial position, because that's core to their philosophy of self-refinement, but battle with the servants of the Lie is also a major concern for both the Silver Ladder and the Free Council. Mediation and negotiation could be found among the Ladder, Council, and probably the Guardians. Spies will be found among pretty much any order. Espionage is a form of warfare, covering the Arrow's ethos and the Ladder and Council's war against the Exarchs, while the Mysterium protects magic by keeping its secrets hidden and stealing its incarnations out from unworthy hands. Leaders and visionaries are common in both the Ladder and the Council.<br /> <br /> Arrows are the closest to just being &quot;fighters,&quot; but specifically they're a spiritual teaching that <i>strife cultivates understanding</i>.<br /> Thearchs aren't &quot;leaders.&quot; They're a tradition that espouses <i>claiming magic as humanity's birthright,</i> with a belief that <i>arcane understanding dictates authority</i>.<br /> Mystagogues aren't &quot;savants.&quot; They're a religion practicing the <i>worship of magic</i> as a pantheistic oneness, focused on protecting it from the Abyss of un-meaning by <i>keeping manifestations of magic secret</i> from Sleepers and available to the wise Awakened.<br /> Guardians aren't &quot;spies&quot; or &quot;assassins.&quot; They're a messianic cult focused on the <i>moral and responsible use of magic</i> who take on roles as <i>sin-eaters</i> for tasks they don't trust less cautious mages with, using false personas as a way to perform those duties at a remove.<br /> Libertines are a loose association of many different smaller cults and traditions whose chief shared belief is that <i>human culture and life is a font of magical understanding,</i> not received from the Supernal World but springing up through it, and who <i>distrust unchecked authority</i> of any stripe.<br /> <br /> The Arcana are broad in their effects. You won't typically have a mage who boils down just to &quot;fighter&quot; or &quot;talker&quot; or &quot;researcher.&quot; Fighting <i>is</i> research. Spycraft <i>is</i> fighting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-13T13:51:56-07:00","id":1532524,"title":"","content":"Trying to compare Exalted types to the Paths also doesn't really work since there are nine main types of Exalted (plus the unique Exigents, and additional optional groups) to five Paths.<br /> <br /> Even if one wanted to go back to the &quot;roots&quot; of Exalted and the first five primary Exalted playable types, you're swapping the Dragonblooded out for the Infernals; which feels a bit more like confirmation bias than a real pattern (even more so if you consider that the concept of Infernals as their own unique type of Exalted makes them they seventh group introduce, and only at the end of 2e).<br /> <br /> It's just not a good fit. For example, look at the Moros. Sure there's the obvious death-themes to link them to the Abyssals, but the Liminals are also connected to death. There's also the Alchemicals who might not have a direct connection to the Underworld, but are certainly reflective of the Matter side of the equation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}